e service was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 45386, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016qEnXPhp5RFkhjHn169nZm", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_timeout"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 45386, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016qEnXPhp5RFkhjHn169nZm", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 48781, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Cause:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions now run it, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovered metrics. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FBv48DGKwvEuVRJTzXbvhu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014oifLSYBmiJADiwhwvgdE3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01K5xzCGZ7uqvXzd7kCNs7nA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01H98fwCxPBc5qGkHGYXgSj1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016tAu7Eppe8z4uRPQzSPkmR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016qEnXPhp5RFkhjHn169nZm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. The service was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Cause:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions now run it, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovered metrics. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}